    {
      "name": "check_layout",
      "description": "Use when a plan only needs checking, without making a link or a drawing: returns the same issues as create_plan. The plan format is in create_plan's description.\nReturns {ok, issues, summary}; ok is true when no issue is an error or a warning. Each issue is {code, severity, message, ids}, ids naming the piece first, then what it hits. Errors: item_overlap, item_outside_room (outside every room). Warnings: door_blocked (a piece in a door's swing or track), doorway_blocked (in the passage either side of a door), opening_overlap, opening_off_wall, room_overlap, window_between_rooms, unknown_field (a key the format lacks, usually a typo). Info: tight_clearance, a straight gap from 6 in / 15 cm up to minClearance (in the plan's unit, default 24 in / 61 cm) between two pieces or a piece and a wall; closer pieces (chairs at a table) are taken as meant. Messages name rooms, pieces by label (with their centre when labels repeat) and doors by where they are on the wall.",
